    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I feel this problem is due to character encoding problem. <div><br></div><div>It&#39;s saying, the local of your computer is different with the local on the server you deployed. </div><div><br></div><div>Have a look these two blogs, which may be helpful: </div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"http://withr.me/understand-encoding-garbed-text/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://withr.me/understand-encoding-garbed-text/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792395323793000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3WJg0gHb9prd7-fS9-ZviP\">http://withr.me/understand-encoding-garbed-text/</a><br></div><div><a href=\"http://withr.me/configure-character-encoding-for-r-under-linux-and-windows/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://withr.me/configure-character-encoding-for-r-under-linux-and-windows/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792395323793000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3XwX7C2waIqswwRn15f1R7\">http://withr.me/configure-character-encoding-for-r-under-linux-and-windows/</a><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Gook luck!</div></div>"
    ],
    [
